# deploy/crontab
#
# Managed crontab entries for the Oceanovia application.
#
# Install with:  bash deploy/install-cron.sh
#
# The block between the markers is managed by deploy/install-cron.sh. The
# installer removes a previously installed block before it appends the current
# one, so it can be run repeatedly without creating duplicate entries. Every
# crontab entry outside the block is left untouched.
#
# Placeholders: @APP_DIR@ (the application directory) and @PHP_BIN@ (the PHP
# executable) are resolved by the installer.

# BEGIN oceanovia managed entries

# Weekly full backup (Sunday 2am)
0 2 * * 0 "@APP_DIR@/deploy/backup.sh" >> "@APP_DIR@/storage/logs/backup.log" 2>&1

# Laravel scheduler (every minute).
#
# It runs the tasks that are registered in routes/console.php, which includes
# the daily dry run of money:reconcile-procurement-settlements at 03:15 UTC.
# The scheduler never runs that reconciliation in write mode: the registered
# task always passes --dry-run, and a repair is a separate, explicit
# "money:reconcile-procurement-settlements --write" run.
#
# The output of the scheduler is appended to storage/logs/scheduler.log. That
# file needs log rotation; see docs/PROCUREMENT_SETTLEMENT_RUNBOOK.md.
* * * * * cd "@APP_DIR@" && "@PHP_BIN@" artisan schedule:run >> "@APP_DIR@/storage/logs/scheduler.log" 2>&1

# END oceanovia managed entries
